    "Description": "WebKitGTK+ is port of the WebKit portable web rendering engine to the GTK+ platform. These packages provide WebKitGTK+ for GTK+ 3.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* chromium-browser: angle: ANGLE in Google Chrome: Information disclosure via out-of-bounds read (CVE-2026-87596)\n\n* chromium-browser: angle: ANGLE in Google Chrome: Arbitrary code execution via crafted HTML page (CVE-2026-87500)\n\n* chromium-browser: angle: Chromium: Arbitrary code execution via buffer overflow in ANGLE (CVE-2026-87654)\n\n* chromium-browser: angle: Google Chrome (ANGLE): Arbitrary Code Execution vulnerability (CVE-2026-87621)\n\n* chromium-browser: angle: Chromium-browser: Arbitrary code execution via use-after-free vulnerability in ANGLE (CVE-2026-87512)\n\n* chromium-browser: angle: ANGLE: Arbitrary code execution in Google Chrome due to use-after-free (CVE-2026-87648)\n\n* chromium-browser: angle: ANGLE in Google Chrome: Information disclosure via crafted HTML page (CVE-2026-87602)\n\n* chromium-browser: angle: ANGLE in Google Chrome: Information disclosure via crafted HTML page (CVE-2026-87586)\n\n* chromium-browser: angle: ANGLE in Google Chrome: Arbitrary code execution via out-of-bounds read (CVE-2026-87604)\n\n* chromium-browser: angle: chromium-browser: Improper input validation in ANGLE (CVE-2026-91738)\n\n* chromium-browser: angle: chromium-browser: Uninitialized resource in ANGLE (CVE-2026-91720)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* webkitgtk4 2.54.0 regression breaks Eclipse IDE WebKit [rhel-7-els] (JIRA:RHEL-300676)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
